gitcha-medic watches the Gitcha server on this machine, the Apache Cassandra node it keeps its database in, and
the nginx (or Caddy) in front, and says in plain words what is wrong and why.

  sudo gitcha-medic                 look and say (exit 0 all well, 1 something is wrong)
  sudo gitcha-medic --heal          also run the safe remedies: start a stopped service, restart a stuck one
  sudo gitcha-medic --ask           also consult the configured agent
  sudo gitcha-medic --list          every remedy, with its class
  sudo gitcha-medic --yes NAME      run one remedy of class confirm, after reading what it does
  sudo gitcha-medic --json          the facts and findings for a program (C4OK's Operations door, for one)
  journalctl -t gitcha-medic        what it has said to syslog

The timer (gitcha-medic.timer, every five minutes, enabled when debconf was told to) runs it with --quiet: syslog
hears every run; the rooms hear a change, or a heartbeat every GITCHA_MEDIC_REPEAT (6 h).

Three classes of remedy, and the line between them is the consent gate:
  safe     start or restart a service.  Runs from the timer only when GITCHA_MEDIC_HEAL=safe; an agent may ask for one.
  confirm  moves data or edits a file (for example, move an empty Cassandra data directory aside so the node starts
           under a new cluster_name).  Runs only when a person types --yes NAME; the medic and any agent can only ask.
  manual   hands only: the medic says what it sees and what to try.
Nothing the medic does deletes data, edits gitcha.env or debconf.env, or touches secret.key.

Settings: /etc/inputloop/gitcha/medic.env (root only; every setting is listed there with its default), written by
  dpkg-reconfigure inputloop-gitcha-medic
Channels: syslog, tavern (POST /api/say on this machine's Tavern, token from its agent.json), chadgram (one ilmsg/1
line per message in a JSONL file), webhook (JSON by POST), c4 (a postcard file in a folder).  comic.chat and the Wire
are named in the design and wait for adapters.

The agent (GITCHA_MEDIC_AGENT): none by default; claude speaks to the Claude API with a key in
/etc/inputloop/gitcha/agent.key (mode 600, read per call).  It sees redacted facts (no setting's value, no key) and may
ask for safe remedies; it cannot say yes for a person.  local, inputloop and openai are reserved names (TODO).
